cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use vram-fit in research or teaching, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "vram-fit: Exact VRAM and Throughput Estimation for Local Large Language Model Inference and Parameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning"
abstract: >-
  vram-fit computes the GPU memory required to run or fine-tune a transformer language model
  on given hardware, without downloading model weights. It reads only the model's config.json or
  GGUF/safetensors headers, reconstructs a per-tensor inventory, applies the byte-exact layout of
  quantization formats (llama.cpp k-quant mixing rules, AWQ, GPTQ, EXL2, FP8, NF4, MXFP4), and models
  the KV cache (GQA, MQA, MLA, sliding-window and hybrid recurrent layers, KV quantization),
  engine-specific activation buffers, driver overhead and LoRA/QLoRA/full fine-tuning optimizer state.
  It probes NVIDIA (NVML), AMD (ROCm) and Apple Silicon hardware, predicts decode and prefill
  throughput from memory bandwidth and compute, and searches for the fastest configuration that does
  not exceed device memory, emitting launch commands for llama.cpp, Ollama, vLLM, ExLlamaV2 and Unsloth.
authors:
  - alias: "GinckL"
repository-code: "https://github.com/GinckL/vram-fit"
url: "https://github.com/GinckL/vram-fit"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-04"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - GPU memory estimation
  - VRAM calculator
  - KV cache
  - quantization
